  <issue>
  [PERF] compute `dtypes` when performing binary operations
It should be possible and beneficial to compute `dtypes` when doing binary operations without remote calls so other subsequent operations, which require `dypes` to be known, do not perform the remote calls to compute it.

Here are some examples when we can compute/pass known dtypes to the core dataframe.

1. `left_df + right_df`, leftleft_df.dtypes and right_df.dtypes are known and equal to each other
2. `left_df + 1`, left_df.dtypes is known, dtype of 1 is int.
  </issue>
  
